\begin{abstract}
We present the Autonomous Dark Domain Engine (ADDE-v4), a distributed and
privacy-preserving computational framework designed for real-time analysis of
next-generation astrophysical survey data. ADDE-v4 integrates AMR+PM+Octree
N-body solvers with CKKS fully homomorphic encryption, enabling secure
evaluation of weak-lensing shear fields, BAO correlation functions, and
generative anomaly metrics across 16{,}384 encrypted SIMD channels. Performance
tests demonstrate stable evolution of $16{,}384^3$ particles, InfiniBand
saturation at $97.8\%$, and automated cryptographic bootstrapping at
multiplicative depth~12. Under extreme observational noise ($30\%$ intrinsic
shape noise, $25\%$ masking), ADDE-v4 reconstructs convergence maps with
$\mathrm{SNR}=8.42$ and identifies injected dark-sector perturbations at
$5.12\sigma$. These results establish ADDE-v4 as a validated, real-time
computational instrument for dark matter and dark energy studies in upcoming
wide-field surveys.
\end{abstract}